[32m+[m[32m## SSH[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mConnections of type `ssh` use these options (all optional, set in the connection's `Options`):[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| Option | Default | Meaning |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|---|[m
[32m+[m[32m| `username` | none | Used when no saved credential supplies one |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `privateKeyPath` | none | Log in with a key; the credential's password is then the key passphrase |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `term` | `xterm-256color` | Terminal type requested from the server |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `keepAliveSeconds` | `30` | `0` turns keep-alive off (max 3600) |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `connectTimeoutSeconds` | `15` | 1 to 300 |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe port defaults to 22. Host keys use trust on first use: unknown keys and changed keys always ask, and with no prompt available they are refused. Trusted keys are remembered per host and port in `known_hosts.json`.[m
